LAMMPS (10 Dec 2025)
KOKKOS mode with Kokkos version 4.7.1 is enabled
  using double precision
  using view layout = legacy
  will use up to 1 GPU(s) per node
WARNING: When using a single thread, the Kokkos Serial backend (i.e. Makefile.kokkos_mpi_only) gives better performance than the OpenMP backend (src/KOKKOS/kokkos.cpp:266)
  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
package kokkos
package kokkos neigh half newton on
# =============================================================================
# LAMMPS input script for Water Box NVT Prerelaxation using MACE
# =============================================================================

units           metal
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
atom_style      atomic
atom_modify     map yes
newton          on

read_data       water_box.lmpdat
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0.89414363 0.77546488 0) to (21.105856 18.304498 8.4436268)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  300 atoms
  read_data CPU = 0.015 seconds

# Use dynamic model path passed from command line via -var MODEL_PT_PATH
pair_style      mliap unified ${MODEL_PT_PATH} 0
pair_style      mliap unified mace_pretained_models/mace-mh-1.model_omol.pt 0
pair_coeff      * * O H

thermo          100
thermo_style    custom step cpu spcpu temp press pe ke etotal vol density fmax fnorm
thermo_modify   flush yes

# --- Key parameters ---
variable        dt_val equal 0.0005    # 0.5 fs timestep
variable        tdamp equal 0.05       # 100 * dt

# =============================================================================
# Trajectory dump
# =============================================================================
dump            xyz_traj all xyz 100 trajectory_water.xyz
dump_modify     xyz_traj element O H

dump            lmp_traj all custom 100 trajectory_water.lammpstrj id type x y z
dump_modify     lmp_traj sort id

# =============================================================================
# Phase 1: Energy Minimization
# =============================================================================
print "Phase 1: Energy Minimization"
Phase 1: Energy Minimization
minimize        0.0 1.0e-8 5000 50000

